Set the new node’s click handler, then update the listeners. `updateDOMListeners` handles normalizing the event and replacing any previous click handler:

```js
newVirtualNode.data ??= {};
newVirtualNode.data.on ??= {};
newVirtualNode.data.on.click = handleClick;

updateDOMListeners(oldVirtualNode, newVirtualNode);
```

Make sure `newVirtualNode.elm` refers to the DOM element whose listeners should be updated.

Assuming you have a list of games with a `year` field, here’s a JavaScript function that returns the games from 2019:

```javascript
function getGamesOf2019(games) {
  return games.filter(game => game.year === 2019);
}
```

For example, `getGamesOf2019([{ title: "Game A", year: 2019 }, { title: "Game B", year: 2020 }])` returns Game A. If you meant games from a particular sport or an online game database, let me know which one.

